    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Task 1: value iteration for a small discrete MDP\n",
        "using 4x4 FrozenLake with is_slippery=False because it's a small, discrete, deterministic environment that makes the MDP easy to define, interpret, and visualize.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hfxcy4YEe-jG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Clearly define the state space, action space, reward structure, and discount factor\n",
        "**structure**  \n",
        "- map size: 4x4\n",
        "- transitions: deterministic with is_slippery=False\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**state space**\n",
        "- each grid cell is a state\n",
        "- 4x4 grid --> 16 total states numbered 0-15\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**action space**\n",
        "- 4 actions:\n",
        "  - 0 = left\n",
        "  - 1 = down\n",
        "  - 2 = right\n",
        "  - 3 = up\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**reward structure**\n",
        "- reaching goal has a reward of 1\n",
        "- all other transitions have no reward (0)\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**discount factor**\n",
        "- gamma = 0.95\n",
        "- FrozenLake works better with higher gamma values because the reward is only received at the end goal, so the agent must strongly value future over short-term reward. Gamma of 0.95 allows the agent to value long-term rewards while still slightly decreasing the reward with each additional step, so shorter paths to the end goal are preferred over long ones."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZPh39iR0jNR9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Implement value iteration and compute final policy"
      ],
